From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rumisle <why-excuse-quail@duck.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:07:31 +0800
Subject: server/auth: give the web app's authenticated requests the session
 cookie

The web app sends the password (or a pairing token) in a header, which a page load can't do, so
every link it opens on the server (a file under /api/fs/read, a download) got the Basic challenge.
Same-origin requests that pass with credentials but carry no valid session cookie now also get the
cookie that pairing links set (same name, HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, 30 days, signed with the
password), so those page loads are signed in too. Cross-site requests and API clients get none.

Ocelot-Patch: server/session-cookie

diff --git a/packages/server/src/middleware/authorization.ts b/packages/server/src/middleware/authorization.ts
